for qid,reason in {
'0301-Q04':'Recognizing R*0=0 and distinguishing an observer from an expression basis is a short conceptual check, not a multi-stage hard derivation.',
'0303-Q04':'This directly recalls the explicitly defined shorthand observer U versus expression frame A.',
'0315-Q05':'This is the standard local-linearization versus exact-instantaneous-derivative distinction with no demanding calculation.',
'0316-Q02':'This tests the simple conditional nature of configuration/time dependence.',
'0318-Q04':'This is a single application of rank preservation under invertible multiplication.',
'0319-Q02':'The item asks for the definition of task-Jacobian singularity, not a difficult rank calculation.',
'0319-Q03':'This is a direct representation-versus-physical-direction distinction.',
'0319-Q05':'The supplied diagonal 2-by-2 map makes compatibility evident from one zero row.',
'0319-Q09':'The two independent columns are explicit coordinate unit vectors; the rank calculation is one step.',
'0322-Q04':'Exact model differentiation versus model fidelity is a basic conceptual qualification.',
'0323-Q03':'Checking whether a matrix is square is not a hard determinant or rank problem.'}.items():flag(qid,'difficulty','Change difficulty from hard to medium. '+reason)
flag('0319-Q08','difficulty','Change extremely_tricky to hard at most (medium is defensible). The identity derivative is immediate; the useful joint-limit-versus-rank distinction does not require an exceptionally tricky calculation. Retain the explicit ambient-map and inequality assumptions.')
# Formula sheet items must explain their actual symbols and bases, not generic replacements.
flag('0299-Q02','explanation','Define vx, vy and vz individually as Cartesian velocity components in the same specified reference/basis, and speed as their nonnegative norm, all in m/s. The current variables record defines only generic v, which is not the expression symbol.')
for short in ['0306-Q02','0310-Q02']:
 flag(short,'explanation','Make formula metadata self-contained: define v_Q^A (point Q velocity relative A in A components), v_origin^A (B-origin velocity relative A in A components), v_relative^B (Q relative B expressed B), q_B (B-origin-to-Q offset in B components), omega^A and R_AB. On P0306 also state explicitly that constant relative orientation makes omega_AB=0, so the general transport formula reduces to the stated two-term case.')
for short in ['0312-Q05','0313-Q03','0313-Q04','0314-Q03','0314-Q04']:
 flag(short,'explanation','Replace generic omega/v definitions in formula metadata with actual omega_parent, omega_child, v_parent and v_child definitions: identify the fixed base observer, the corresponding link/origin, and parent/child expression basis. Define z_child as the joint-axis unit vector expressed in the child basis and preserve the stated frame-placement conditions. Keep all formulas independently understandable in a formula sheet.')
flag('0318-Q03','explanation','Define twist_A and twist_B explicitly as the same observer/physical-point stacked [linear; angular] velocity in A and B bases; define R_AB direction. Repair severely joined prose such as "xmaps toy" and "MultiplythesameRby" throughout this item.')
flag('0321-Q03','explanation','Define q_dot as the computed joint-coordinate time derivative and q_next as the next-step coordinate state, with explicit units. They are used in the formula but omitted from its variable definitions.')
flag('0315-Q04','explanation','Repair the self-contained map assumption "SameexplicitmapF... dimensionlesscoordinates" into normal spaced prose. The map and given point must remain intelligible when the question is shuffled away from its preceding example; keep all numerical values and equations unchanged.')
flag('0314-Q01','assumptions','Use the unambiguous first-derivative notation d_dot or dotted d, not "ddot" in o2. The current spelling conventionally suggests a second derivative; distinguish linear joint speed from acceleration and angular velocity.')
flag('0314-Q03','assumptions','Replace "prismatic ddot=4 m/s" and "Addddot" by an explicitly defined d_dot=4 m/s, first time derivative of displacement. Also repair joined workings. Units resolve the intended answer, but the current spelling unnecessarily suggests acceleration.')
flag('0314-Q04','explanation','Repair severely joined assumption/working text ("Atthisinstant", "unchangedbecauseR=I", "CoincidentoriginsmakeP=0", "Addtheprismaticlinearvelocity"). Keep the explicit zero parent-origin velocity, P=0 and R=I premises.')
flag('0313-Q04','explanation','Repair "Same numericparentdata" and "Multiplytoget" into readable prose. Preserve the full numerical parent data in assumptions so the shuffled item does not depend on a preceding question.')
flag('0322-Q05','explanation','Use null-space joint RATE, not joint increment, when claiming zero task velocity. Qualify the o2 explanation as zero instantaneous primary-task velocity; a finite joint displacement in a local null space need not preserve the finite task pose for nonlinear kinematics.')
# Explicit conflicts may not be accepted just because the derived key is correct.
conflicts={
'0316-Q02':'Time variation is conditional on q(t) and J(q), not mandatory for every entry/trajectory.',
'0319-Q02':'Task singularity is a drop below attainable regular rank, not loss of physical joints or necessarily one named axis.',
'0319-Q03':'A lost direction can be a basis-dependent linear combination of axes; coordinate rotation does not restore rank.',
'0319-Q06':'At exact rank loss, compatible targets can have finite solutions while incompatible targets have no exact solution. This differs from a divergent near-singular inverse limit.',
'0319-Q10':'The modeled differential-task singularity is diagnosed by its Jacobian rank; other failures need separate model/singularity definitions.',
'0321-Q06':'An explicit Jacobian provides local interpretability, not unconditional physical safety without constraints, valid models and controller checks.',
'0323-Q03':'Ordinary determinant testing is restricted to square maps; rectangular maps need rank analysis. Narrow conflict roles to the actual overbroad statements rather than implying every cited equation is wrong.'}
for short,why in conflicts.items():flag(short,'sourceSupport','Add version-bound question-level conflictResolution identifying the literal source claim, the bounded correction and derivation/source basis. The citation already has role=conflict but there is no resolution metadata; the shared gate correctly excludes it. '+why+' Preserve the source-dispute ledger and do not mark the underlying PDF globally resolved.')
for short in ['0316-Q03','0316-Q04']:
 flag(short,'sourceSupport','The p316 citation is labeled explicit support although its "most general 6x6" statement contradicts the general 6xn answer. Retain p323 as clear supporting evidence and either remove the incidental p316 citation or mark its conflicting statement with explicit version-bound resolution. Do not silently treat the contradiction as agreeing evidence.')
now=datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).isoformat();reviews=[];reviewer=blind['reviewerId']
for qid,q in qs.items():
 a=answers[qid];checks={k:True for k in CHECK_KEYS}
 for f in flags.get(qid,[]):checks[f['check']]=False
 assert reviewer not in {q['authorId'],*q.get('revisionAuthors',[])}
 refs=q['citations'];reason=a['reasoning']+' After freezing the source-first answer, I inspected all keyed explanations, steps, formula metadata, assumptions and citations. The answer agrees; outstanding source bindings, quality, difficulty or readability findings are recorded separately. The independent numerical script checks transport derivatives, recurrences, basis changes, chain rule, rank, null-space and virtual-power cases. Numerical variants are explicitly given rather than asserted to be slide examples.'
 reviews.append({'id':f'REV-{qid}-v1-interface-independent','questionId':qid,'questionVersion':q['version'],'questionSha256':question_hash(q),'reviewerId':reviewer,'decision':'flagged' if qid in flags else 'verified','reviewedAt':now,'sourceVersions':{c['sourceId']:c['sourceSha256'] for c in refs},'reviewedSlideIds':a['reviewedSlideIds'],'sourceInspectionEvidence':[{'physicalPage':c['physicalPage'],'inspectorIds':[reviewer],'previewSha256':hashlib.sha256((ROOT/f"sources/previews/lectures/page-{c['physicalPage']:04d}.webp").read_bytes()).hexdigest()} for c in refs],'independentAnswerOptionIds':a['independentAnswerOptionIds'],'solvedBeforeAnswerSeen':True,'checks':checks,'reasoning':reason,'findings':[f['finding'] for f in flags.get(qid,[])],'reviewType':'independent_blind_initial_review','priorReviewerExposure':False,'priorAuthorExposure':False,'blindAnswersPath':str(blindpath.relative_to(ROOT)),'blindAnswersSha256':hashlib.sha256(blindpath.read_bytes()).hexdigest(),'computationsPath':'audits/W02-L09-independent-computations.json'})
reviewpath=ROOT/'data/reviews/W02-L09-v1-independent.json';assert not reviewpath.exists();reviewpath.write_text(json.dumps(reviews,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\n')
gaps=[{'physicalPage':309,'kind':'diagram interpretation','gap':'The O/A/B/C geometric labels are not directly discriminated. Existing radius and displacement questions establish the algebra but not identification of OA (axis projection), AB/AC (perpendicular radius), OB/OC (old/new full point vectors), and BC (finite tip chord). Add a source-figure mapping or match-the-following item to distinguish the circular radius from full |Q|, keeping the small-angle qualification.','status':'new draft question required'}, {'physicalPage':321,'kind':'application/source recall','gap':'The explicit usefulness/application bullet (simple and efficient, industrial robot teleoperation and AI manipulation) lacks direct coverage. An application-selection item could distinguish velocity-level online control from a one-shot static pose solve; avoid universal performance claims.','status':'new draft question required'}, {'physicalPage':322,'kind':'table comparison','gap':'The traditional-column Jacobian-based singularity-avoidance bullet is not directly covered as a control use. Existing p319 questions diagnose singularity; add a bounded item distinguishing avoiding problematic configurations from changing the mechanism rank by relabeling axes or assuming neural control eliminates singularities.','status':'new draft question required'}]
summary={'reviewedAt':now,'reviewed':102,'verified':102-len(flags),'flagged':len(flags),'answerAgreement':102,'answerCorrectionsRequired':0,'independentBlindReview':True,'sourcePagesInspected':list(range(296,326)),'computationGroupsPassed':7,'computationCasesPassed':5026,'reviewPath':str(reviewpath.relative_to(ROOT)),'blindAnswersPath':str(blindpath.relative_to(ROOT)),'actionableFlags':flags,'flagCountsByCheck':dict(collections.Counter(f['check'] for ff in flags.values() for f in ff)),'approvedCurrentHashes':{r['questionId']:r['questionSha256'] for r in reviews if r['decision']=='verified'},'allReviewedCurrentHashes':{r['questionId']:r['questionSha256'] for r in reviews},'coverageGaps':gaps,'nonblockingStyleNotes':['Many minor English/number joins remain even outside the specifically unreadable flagged workings. Do not silently polish accepted objects; any later prose change must version-bump and rebind the review.','The source-issue ledger itself contains heavily joined words. It should be made human-readable without altering the recorded source disputes or claiming a global source resolution.'],'sourceAndScopeNotes':['The original packet contained citation evidence text; the reviewer removed it before solving and inspected source pixels directly.','Page 321 combining overdots exist in encoded PDF text although poorly rendered in previews. This is a rendering qualification, not a newly invented missing-dot source error.','All 102 keys agree, but matching keys alone does not resolve the seven missing explicit conflict bindings or other quality flags.','No authored question, inspection record, source-dispute ledger, source PDF, or canonical bank was changed.']}
(ROOT/'audits/W02-L09-independent-summary.json').write_text(json.dumps(summary,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\n');(ROOT/'audits/W02-L09-independent-coverage-gaps.json').write_text(json.dumps(gaps,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\n')
print(json.dumps({k:summary[k] for k in ['reviewed','verified','flagged','answerAgreement','flagCountsByCheck','computationCasesPassed']},indent=2))
